# Security Checklist (Cursor mirror of rules/11-security-checklist.md)

> Canonical source: `rules/11-security-checklist.md`. If they differ, canonical wins.

Ship only after all 20 pass: 1 security headers (CSP/HSTS/nosniff, `poweredByHeader: false`) · 2 race conditions (atomic DB ops, no check-then-act) · 3 `.git` not deployed (verify `/.git/config` → 404) · 4 account pre-hijacking (verified email + provider as identity) · 5 Supabase storage (private buckets, RLS, server-side validation) · 6 subdomain takeover (no dangling DNS) · 7 price never from browser (recompute server-side) · 8 SSRF (no user-supplied URL fetches, block metadata IP) · 9 credential stuffing (rate limits, generic errors, MFA) · 10 path traversal (allowlisted base dir, normalized paths) · 11 open database (RLS every table, service key server-only, no NEXT_PUBLIC_ secrets) · 12 reset poisoning (base URL from config, never Host header) · 13 no polyfill.io / uncontrolled CDNs (self-host + SRI) · 14 no prod source maps · 15 SMS pumping (per-phone + per-IP OTP limits, fraud guard) · 16 clickjacking (X-Frame-Options / frame-ancestors) · 17 prompt injection (model output = untrusted data) · 18 open redirect (relative-path / host allowlist only) · 19 JWT secrets (≥256-bit random, server env, verify iss/aud/exp) · 20 user enumeration (generic responses, constant-time).

Rules:

- Client-sent values are display hints, never trust (price, path, redirect, identity).
- Verify exact config keys in framework docs — never invent config.
- Report gate status in the response before finishing.
